lisa-design:
- The tracking issue is the only store: the state is JSON in an HTML comment at the end of the body (json.Marshal escapes < and >, so it can't close the comment). No other storage.
- Phase (progress) and Hold (blocked / needs-human) are separate fields. Holds are recomputed from GitHub on every run, except Sticky ones (a failed ccf-bump), which wait for /retry.
- EvaluateChecks uses the latest check of each name; the required check (ci / required) must be present and pass.
- The interfaces follow the tokens: Repos (release bot, scoped to the train's repos), Tracker (GITHUB_TOKEN, issues in workflows), Members (optional org-members-read token).
